  main.innerHTML=`<section class="intro"><p class="kicker">Findings from company filings</p><h1>How businesses earn money.<br>What their accounts leave unclear.</h1><p>Explore the changes affecting companies, understand how each business works, and examine whether reported profits turn into cash after its costs and obligations.</p><p class="meta">Start with a theme, choose a specific question, then read the company evidence. These are research interpretations; unresolved questions remain visible in the articles.</p><p class="library-stats"><span>${counts.Company} company studies</span><span>${counts.Explanation} business explanations</span><span>${counts.Comparison} comparisons</span><a href="#findings-heading">Read four findings</a><a href="#trends">Read the broader trends</a><a href="#library">Browse the full library</a></p></section><section id="trends" class="trend-bridge" aria-labelledby="trends-heading"><p class="kicker">A second reading layer</p><h2 id="trends-heading">What repeated across the filings?</h2><p class="trend-bridge-intro">The company dossiers and comparisons explain one business at a time. The separate trend archive looks across 519 annual reports and recent earnings to identify recurring economic, demographic, cultural, industrial and regulatory patterns.</p><div class="trend-bridge-grid"><a href="/site/trends/ai-infrastructure-toll.html"><span class="label">Technology · infrastructure</span><strong>AI infrastructure: who controls the inputs?</strong><span>Who controls the physical inputs, and who carries the labor and capacity burden?</span></a><a href="/site/trends/gray-wave-dividend.html"><span class="label">Demographics · healthcare</span><strong>Aging and healthcare demand</strong><span>How aging turns recurring care, equipment and logistics into revenue.</span></a><a href="/site/trends/affordability-ceiling.html"><span class="label">Consumer · economics</span><strong>Consumer demand by budget</strong><span>Why demand is separating by customer budget rather than moving together.</span></a><a href="/site/trends/private-capital-colonization.html"><span class="label">Finance · regulation</span><strong>Credit moving outside banks</strong><span>What moves outside banks when capital and obligations migrate to private platforms.</span></a><a href="/site/trends/grids-new-landlords.html"><span class="label">Energy · infrastructure</span><strong>Who pays for new power infrastructure?</strong><span>Who funds and owns the wires, generation and fuel routes behind new load.</span></a><a href="/site/trends/cash-harvest.html"><span class="label">Capital allocation · consumer</span><strong>When mature businesses return cash</strong><span>When pricing power and captive demand become distributions instead of reinvestment.</span></a></div><p><a href="/site/trends/index.html">Open all 20 trends and their 168 sub-pages →</a></p></section><section id="themes" aria-labelledby="themes-heading" class="themes"><div class="themes-heading"><p class="kicker">Browse by economic question</p><h2 id="themes-heading">Choose a theme, then a company.</h2><p>Each theme gathers a few basic questions and the company studies that test them. Start with the question that interests you; the studies supply the filings, cash calculations and open tests.</p></div>${themes.map((t,i)=>`<section class="theme"><p class="kicker">Theme ${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</p><h2>${t.title}</h2><p>${t.intro}</p><ul class="subthemes">${t.topics.map(([name,slug])=>`<li>${link(name,fp(slug))}</li>`).join('')}</ul><p class="label">Company studies</p><div class="cases">${t.companies.map(([name,slug])=>link(name,company(slug))).join('')}</div></section>`).join('')}</section><section id="library" class="library"><h2>Find a company or a question</h2><p>The full library includes company studies, explanations of business models, and comparisons across companies. Article depth and reporting dates vary. The main reader currently contains ${counts.Company} deep company studies; the <a href="/site/cross-framework-companies/index.html">company coverage index</a> contains 238 company pages, including shorter roster-level packet pages. Each result shows how many of the five questions it addresses.</p><div class="controls"><label for="search" class="label">Search article titles</label><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Try Chipotle, insurance or electricity"></div><div class="filters" aria-label="Article type">${['All','Company','Explanation','Comparison'].map((k,i)=>`<button data-kind="${k}" aria-pressed="${i===0}">${k==='All'?'All articles':k==='Company'?'Company studies':k==='Explanation'?'Business explanations':'Comparisons'}</button>`).join('')}<button data-coverage="complete" aria-pressed="false">Pages addressing all five questions</button></div><p id="count" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="meta"></p><ul id="results" class="results"></ul></section>`;
  document.querySelector('.trend-bridge .kicker').textContent='Across the companies';
  document.querySelector('.intro .meta').insertAdjacentHTML('afterend','<p class="method-link"><a href="?file=analysis/cross-sector/combined-end-to-end-forensic-research-system-2026-09-13.md">How to read the research: from filing facts to cash, risks, and future tests →</a></p>');
  document.querySelector('#trends-heading').textContent='What kept recurring across the filings?';
  document.querySelector('.trend-bridge-intro').textContent='The company dossiers and comparisons explain one business at a time. The trend pages read across 519 annual reports and recent earnings to identify recurring economic, demographic, cultural, industrial and regulatory patterns.';
  document.querySelector('.themes').insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin',`<section class="featured-findings" aria-labelledby="findings-heading"><h2 id="findings-heading">Five findings from the research</h2><p class="meta">Examples from the linked company studies. Each study provides the source trail, later updates and limits of the analysis.</p><div class="findings-grid">${findings.map(f=>{const target=f.path||company(f.slug);return `<article><p class="kicker">${esc(f.company)} · ${esc(f.period)}</p><h3>${link(f.title,target)}</h3><p>${esc(f.fact)}</p><p>${esc(f.meaning)}</p><p class="open-question"><span class="label">The unresolved question</span><br>${esc(f.question)}</p>${link('Read the '+f.company+' analysis',target)}</article>`}).join('')}</div></section>`);
  document.querySelector('.featured-findings').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<p>${link('Read the cross-industry explanation: who keeps the cash?','analysis/cross-sector/control-point-versus-burden-carrier-synthesis-2026-09-13.md')}</p>`);
  document.querySelector('#findings-heading').textContent='Five findings from the research';
  document.querySelector('.library-stats a[href="#findings-heading"]').textContent='Read five findings';
  document.querySelector('.featured-findings').insertAdjacentHTML('afterend',`<section class="foundations" aria-labelledby="foundations-heading"><p class="kicker">Start with the concepts</p><h2 id="foundations-heading">Seven short explanations before the company studies</h2><p class="meta">These pages define the questions used across the archive. They are written for readers who want the reasoning made explicit before reading the filings.</p><div class="foundation-grid">${foundations.map(([title,intro,path])=>`<article><h3>${link(title,path)}</h3><p>${esc(intro)}</p></article>`).join('')}</div></section>`);
  document.querySelector('#foundations-heading').textContent='Seven short explanations before the company studies';
  document.querySelector('.featured-findings').insertAdjacentHTML('afterend',`<section class="reading-guide" aria-labelledby="guide-heading"><p class="kicker">A simple reading path</p><h2 id="guide-heading">How to read one study</h2><div class="guide-steps"><p><strong>1. Understand the work.</strong><br>What does the company provide, who pays it and what must happen before the sale is complete?</p><p><strong>2. Follow the money.</strong><br>Read the reported figures, cash bridge and obligations. Check which costs are already included before making an adjustment.</p><p><strong>3. Test the conclusion.</strong><br>Read the evidence that supports the interpretation, then the next filing questions that could change it.</p></div></section>`);
  document.querySelector('.reading-guide').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<details class="coverage-legend"><summary>What are the five core questions?</summary><ul><li><strong>Business economics:</strong> what the company provides, who pays and what must happen before the sale is complete.</li><li><strong>Cash conversion:</strong> how reported activity becomes cash after operating costs, investment and changes in amounts owed or held in stock.</li><li><strong>Risks and accounting tests:</strong> where estimates, obligations, incentives or deal structures could make the reported result less durable.</li><li><strong>Valuation:</strong> what growth, margins and reinvestment assumptions are required by the scenario.</li><li><strong>What to check next:</strong> which future filing or operating measure could strengthen or weaken the conclusion.</li></ul></details>`);
  document.querySelector('.reading-guide').insertAdjacentHTML('afterend',`<section class="method-brief" aria-labelledby="method-heading"><p class="kicker">How the studies are built</p><h2 id="method-heading">One method across different businesses</h2><p class="method-intro">The same questions are applied to a bank, a hospital, a chip company or a restaurant, while the relevant costs and obligations change with the business.</p><div class="method-grid"><p><strong>Liquidity and durability.</strong><br>Can the business keep operating when funding, demand or prices become less favorable? This is the Lyn Alden lens.</p><p><strong>Narrative, reinvestment and value.</strong><br>What must be true for the growth story to produce returns after the money needed to support it? This is the Damodaran lens.</p><p><strong>Earnings quality.</strong><br>Do reported profits become cash, or are timing, estimates, acquisitions, incentives or dilution doing more of the work?</p></div><p>${link('Read the complete research method','analysis/cross-sector/combined-end-to-end-forensic-research-system-2026-09-13.md')} · <a href="/site/cross-framework-companies/index.html">Browse the company coverage index</a></p></section>`);
  document.querySelector('.method-brief').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<p class="method-link">${link('Open the integrated investment-research goal and current synthesis','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-current-synthesis.md')} · ${link('Read the detailed goal specification','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-meaty-end-to-end-goal.md')}</p>`);
  document.querySelector('.method-brief').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<p class="method-link">${link('Open the completion audit','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-completion-audit.md')} · ${link('See the next-evidence queue','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-next-evidence-queue.md')} · ${link('Read the price-implied expectation bridge','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-price-implied-expectation-2026-09-15.md')}</p>`);
  document.querySelector('.method-brief').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<p class="method-link">The three integrated pilots currently contain <strong>226 checked evidence gates</strong>. The ledger verifier confirms structure and arithmetic; qualified and unresolved company tests remain visible in the synthesis. ${link('Read the latest Concord servicing and SEC instrument-observability boundaries','analysis/company-first-principles/capital-flow-apollo-athene-concord-sec-nport-holder-observation-2026-09-16.md')}</p>`);
  document.querySelector('.method-brief').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<details class="proof-grade-legend"><summary>How to read confidence and depth</summary><ul><li><strong>Proven:</strong> the primary source, denominator, and relevant bridge are joined for the stated claim.</li><li><strong>Qualified:</strong> the mechanism or valuation screen is source-backed, but causality, normalization, or future performance remains open.</li><li><strong>Partial:</strong> important activity, cash, or legal-entity facts are visible, but the owner-cash or allocation bridge is incomplete.</li><li><strong>Unresolved:</strong> a decisive source or reconciliation is missing; the claim must not be promoted.</li></ul><p>These labels apply to the integrated pilots in the <a href="/analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-completion-audit.md">completion audit</a> and synthesis. Article coverage counts show depth; source-status lines show what is locally available.</p></details>`);
  document.querySelector('.method-grid p:nth-child(2)').innerHTML='<strong>Narrative, reinvestment and value.</strong><br>What must be true for the growth claim to produce returns after the money needed to support it? This is the Damodaran lens.';
  document.querySelector('.method-brief').insertAdjacentHTML('afterend',`<section id="investment-research" class="investment-research" aria-labelledby="investment-research-heading"><p class="kicker">A connected review path</p><h2 id="investment-research-heading">Integrated investment research</h2><p class="investment-research-intro">This is the deeper end-to-end work: start with the synthesis, open a pilot, inspect the evidence boundary, then use the audit and queue to see what is proven, qualified, partial, or still unresolved.</p><div class="investment-research-grid"><article><p class="state-status">Start here</p><h3>${link('Current synthesis','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-current-synthesis.md')}</h3><p>See how social, macro, industry, filing, owner-cash, valuation and capital-flow evidence is joined into one decision framework.</p></article><article><p class="state-status">Goal and controls</p><h3>${link('Detailed end-to-end goal','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-meaty-end-to-end-goal.md')}</h3><p>Read the acceptance criteria, source architecture, evidence gates, valuation workbenches and promotion rules.</p></article><article><p class="state-status">Pilot 01 · qualified</p><h3>${link('Wheaton–Antamina capital flow','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-pilot-01-wheaton-antamina.md')}</h3><p>Trace the silver stream from asset economics to owner cash, with the BHP-only settlement boundary kept explicit.</p></article><article><p class="state-status">Pilot 02 · qualified</p><h3>${link('Affordability, substitution and retail value','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-pilot-02-affordability-value.md')}</h3><p>Compare value-seeking demand, attached services, capex burden, working capital and normalized cash across the retail cohort.</p></article><article><p class="state-status">Pilot 03 · qualified</p><h3>${link('Apollo–Athene common-owner bridge','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-pilot-03-apollo-athene.md')}</h3><p>Follow origination, buyer-side credit, fee economics and common-owner cash without treating segment screens as statutory returns.</p></article><article><p class="state-status">Theme handoffs</p><h3>${link('Read the source-to-theme handoffs','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-pilot-01-investments-article-handoff.md')}</h3><p>Open the investments-article handoff, IBIS industry handoff, and independent affordability validation that connect external research to filing tests.</p></article></div><p class="investment-research-footer">${link('Open the completion audit','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-completion-audit.md')} · ${link('Review all named deliverables','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-deliverable-audit.md')} · ${link('See the next-evidence queue','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-next-evidence-queue.md')} · ${link('Wheaton reserve-constrained delivery ceiling','analysis/company-first-principles/capital-flow-wheaton-antamina-reserve-constrained-delivery-ceiling-2026-09-15.md')} · ${link('Wheaton upfront settlement bridge','analysis/company-first-principles/capital-flow-wheaton-antamina-bhp-upfront-settlement-bridge-2026-09-16.md')} · ${link('Wheaton after-tax allocation frontier','analysis/company-first-principles/capital-flow-wheaton-antamina-after-tax-financed-allocation-frontier-2026-09-15.md')} · ${link('Apollo Q2 receipt frontier','analysis/company-first-principles/capital-flow-apollo-athene-q2-parent-receipt-attribution-frontier-2026-09-15.md')} · ${link('Retail cash-quality support screen','analysis/company-first-principles/combined-investment-research-pilot-02-retail-cash-quality-support-dependency-2026-09-15.md')}</p></section>`);
  document.querySelector('.method-brief').insertAdjacentHTML('afterend',`<section id="research-state" class="research-state" aria-labelledby="research-state-heading"><p class="kicker">Where the work stands</p><h2 id="research-state-heading">Strong comparisons, open company tests</h2><p class="research-state-intro">Each section below has a working explanation and evidence-backed comparisons. “Current conclusion” means the business mechanism is supported, while some company-level or current-period tests remain open. ${link('Read the full research status','notes/lane-completion-audit-2026-09-14.md')} · <a href="/${encodeURI('notes/valuation-coverage-audit-2026-09-14.md')}">See the valuation coverage map</a>.</p><div class="state-grid">${researchState.map(([title,established,open,path])=>`<article><p class="state-status">Current conclusion</p><h3>${link(title,path)}</h3><p><span class="label">Established</span><br>${esc(established)}</p><p><span class="label">Still open</span><br>${esc(open)}</p></article>`).join('')}</div></section>`);
